e, reference_points and caveats: follow them when explaining it. Scores are compressed near 1.0, so explain results by ranking and by where tiles differ, never as a percentage of 'sameness', and do not name a type of change (the embeddings carry no land-cover labels).", 'tags': ['earth-observation', 'change-detection', 'similarity']}, {'id': 'rank_similar', 'name': 'Rank scenes by similarity', 'description': 'Rank already-embedded scenes by similarity to a reference scene (needs embedding_ids from embed_scene). Each row carries days_apart and caveats; the result carries a reading_guide and reference_points: follow them. Treat near-equal scores (same third decimal) as tied.', 'tags': ['earth-observation', 'similarity', 'retrieval']}]}
